BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pages & Pours: A Reading Night in Sonoma
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260513T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260513T193000
UID:260504SHX9mL_sY0WTVTspt2-z3g
DESCRIPTION:Imagine a night where you can finally sit down\, open your boo
 k\, and just… read.\n\nNo pressure to finish anything. No small talk you
  didn’t sign up for. No agenda you have to keep up with.\n\nJust a glass
  of wine\, a good story\, and a room full of people doing the exact same t
 hing.\n\n**Pages & Pours** is a low-key reading night designed for people 
 who love books\, wine\, and a little breathing room in their week. Bring w
 hatever you’re currently reading\, ease into the evening with a guided w
 ine tasting\, then settle in with a full glass and enjoy a dedicated stret
 ch of uninterrupted reading time. If you feel like it\, there’s space fo
 r easy\, optional conversation—favorite lines\, current reads\, or just 
 a quick hello—and time to linger\, browse the book swap\, or keep readin
 g if you’re in the zone.\n\nThis isn’t about being “on.” It’s ab
 out giving yourself a night that actually feels like yours.\n\nWhether you
  come solo or with a friend\, whether you read one page or fifty\, you’l
 l leave feeling a little more grounded\, a little more inspired\, and alre
 ady looking forward to the next time.\n\n**Your ticket includes a guided w
 ine tasting\, a full glass of wine\, access to the book swap\, and a few e
 xtra thoughtful touches to make the night feel special.**\n\nBring a book 
 to swap (optional\, but encouraged). Bring a friend (or don’t). Just com
 e as you are.
LOCATION:Ram's Gate Winery
URL:https://www.novel-pairings.com/pagespourssonoma
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:36th Annual Spring Art Show
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260513T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260513T170000
UID:260504Fg3OHUksbkStFe-0T-S7sw
DESCRIPTION:The San Geronimo Valley Community Center presents the 36th Ann
 ual Spring Art Show from May 2–17\, 2026 in the Maurice Del Mue Gallerie
 s\,continuing a long-standing West Marin tradition that brings together ov
 er 100 local San Geronimo and Nicasio valley artists across painting\, pho
 tography\, sculpture\, printmaking\, textiles\, ceramics\, and mixed media
 .\n\n The exhibition opens with a public reception on Friday\, May 1st fr
 om 6:30–9pm featuring live music by the Old Time Music Makers. The show
  highlights the creative spirit of West Marin and the important role commu
 nity arts spaces continue to play in connecting people across generations.
 \n\n This year’s exhibition includes work by both emerging and establis
 hed artists and reflects themes of landscape\, ecology\, community\, and c
 onnection to place. The galleries will be open weekdays from 12 - 5:00pm \
 \(please call 415-488-8888 for best viewing times\\) and weekends from 12 
 -6pm. Thank you to Riley Street Art Supplies for their support and to Donn
  DeAngelo for taking the group photo and creating the poster.
LOCATION:San Geronimo Valley Community Center
URL:https://sangeronimovalleycommunitycenter.eventcalendarapp.com/36th-ann
 ual-spring-art-show
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
