BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:S.R. Laws
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260515T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260515T000000
UID:260416XgAXVbf0qEaa9K-1U708Zw
DESCRIPTION:S.R. LAWS IS OUT THERE: He approaches songwriting with a passi
 on for songs that we all grew up on. His sound rings a familiar bell in yo
 ur head while still delivering ideas completely unique.  He draws inspirat
 ion from outstanding storytellers like John Hiatt\, Lou Reed\, Steve Earle
 \, Neil Finn and Ron Sexsmith. All of their music and others have carved a
  deep groove. \n\nGrowing up out there in Northern California\, he develop
 ed a unique connection to music early on. His father worked as a trash col
 lector\, and he would spend hours sifting through bags of discarded 45 rec
 ords. Each find felt like stumbling upon hidden treasures. Some records we
 re covered in dirt and grime\, while others were pristine. The thrill of d
 iscovering new sounds was exhilarating\, and he could hardly wait to drop 
 the needle and immerse himself in the music.\n\nHe embarked on a pilgrimag
 e to Texas with just two suitcases and $500 in his bank account. His goal 
 was to dive into the vibrant music scene and learn from fellow songwriters
 . Austin\, known as the "Live Music Capital of the World\," offered countl
 ess opportunities for him to grow as an artist. Open mics and songwriters'
  nights became his training ground\, where he soaked up every moment\, lis
 tening to others share their stories through music.\n\nThese days\, he res
 ides in Sonoma County\, California\, working hard as a touring artist and 
 singer-songwriter for his original rock band\, The Heartsleeves. He invite
 s everyone to join him on this musical journey\, sharing his songs one per
 son at a time in this vast and unpredictable world we live in.\n\n“Scott
  Ray Laws is an unique and really cool songwriter…he digs into materials
 \, tells a story in his songs\, and has a clean baritone vocality that is 
 easy on the ears. We had a chance to meet and hang with Scott back in May 
 ..and I HAD to have him back for a Wednesday evening.” Luigi- Owner-The 
 Listening Room.\n\n“..An ORIGINAL songwriter who knows how to tell a sto
 ry clearly in song” -  Scotty O’Neill - Guitarist/Promoter\n\n“ It w
 as such a treat catching your set last night — really refreshing to hear
  something new and original. Thanks for pulling up a chair and hanging out
  with us — we really enjoyed the conversation and the stories behind you
 r songs.”  -Tripp B. - Sonoma Songwriter\n\n“Expect slow burning passi
 on and vivid music …the kind of energy that turns into “let’s stay f
 or just one more!..”  - Doug- Owner/Wine Maker- Spicy Vines\n\n“...His
  lyrics simply tell first-person stories from his own life. Nothing fancy\
 , he's not writing to impress--he pours himself\, as is\, into each phrase
  and melody.”- Rebecca Roudman- Dirty Cello Radio Hour KRCB Radio 104.9 
 FM\n\n“ It is through forthright lyrics that are personal and earnest\, 
 that he composes lyrical pictures. Taking snapshots from the most common w
 alks of life...”  - David Sampson - Producer Studio Secti West\n\n“..r
 elaxed mid-tempo Americana\, capturing in each song the rhythmic pocket La
 ws is known for creating.” -  Coyote Music Review 2024
LOCATION:HopMonk Tavern
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108166543?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Floral Fantasia
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260515T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260515T180000
UID:260415BNPMM5xn_kGwichTTgu38g
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  4/14/26\n\n**MAY EXHIBIT: FLORAL
  FANTASIA**\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  April 27  –  May 31\, 2026\n\n**RECEPT
 ION: SATURDAY\, MAY 2\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet BEV HALEY and LUBA 
 STOLPER\;  Learn about their art and celebrate the show.  Be sure to tak
 e part in the Gallery’s free monthlong drawing for a beautiful work by a
  Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.**\n\nSonoma County artist\
 , **Bev Haley\,** unveils new floral works in acrylic that greet Spring wi
 th bountiful blooms and buds guaranteed to warm the viewer’s heart.  De
 signed with a whimsical flare\, each grouping of flowers in these works co
 alesce into harmonious synchronicity.  White and yellow flowers mix it up
  with joyful abandon in “Spring Fling Bouquet.”  A bird joins the par
 ty in “Sunny Side Up\,” a vibrant floral display – reds\, yellows\, 
 blues and more come together like a jeweled mosaic.  “I have always lov
 ed to paint flowers – they’re a simple subject with endless possibilit
 ies\, “noted Haley.  The viewer is rewarded with delicious examples of 
 Haley’s creative approach to those “endless possibilities” with this
  dynamic collection.\n\nPassionate about art\, Haley has tackled multiple 
 subjects but finds herself drawn to flowers.  Her first painting was a si
 ngle daisy in a blue vase.  Working from her reference – books and phot
 os – she composes on the canvas\, creatively applying colors and stylizi
 ng shapes towards a harmonious overall design.  Haley studied art at Sant
 a Rosa J.C. and with multiple master painters.  After retiring from a cha
 llenging business career\, she found her niche in acrylics and mixed media
 .  She has exhibited regionally and in Puerto Vallarta\, Mexico.\n\nMeet 
 the artist: Haley will be hosting the Gallery on May 9 & 23 from 11am to 6
  pm.\n\n The Stairway Smallworks Showcase features **Luba Stolper’s The
  Still Life Tradition\,** a collection of works in oil\, painted in the tr
 aditional style\, building luminosity through time-consuming layers of gla
 zing. One can almost taste the cherries in “Cherry Blossom” or smell t
 he pear in “Night Ritual.”  Masterfully rendered\, these paintings ar
 e so enticing\, one is tempted to reach through the frame to grab a cherry
  to see if it’s real.  Each work seems to capture the viewer in suspend
 ed reality.\n\nMeet the artist: Stolper will be hosting the Gallery on May
  2 & 11 from 11am to 6 pm and May 30 from 11am to 2:30pm.\n\nAlso join us 
 for **ART NITE HEALDSBURG**\, Thursday\, May 7\, 5 – 7 pm.  ART NITE He
 aldsburg\, held the 1st Thursday of Every Month\, is a community event cel
 ebrating art and creativity with over 20 galleries participating.  ArtNit
 eHealdsburg.com.\n\nUpstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Center Street\, Healdsburg\
 , CA 95448. (707) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 pm.    **www.upstai
 rsart gallery.net** \n\nFor further information: Contact: Beverly Bird\, P
 ress Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
