BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Nixil & drouth
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260515T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260515T000000
UID:260224AGz4Ymere0aDsW6s4QGBDg
DESCRIPTION:Born on the cusp of the death of western civilization\, Nixil 
 is a manifestation of chaos\, rage\, strength\, and despair\, channeled th
 rough the art\, magick\, delirium\, and sonic violence of black metal. The
 ir influences range from the weirder side of Mayhem to the atmospheric exp
 ansiveness of French avant garde black metal twisted together and made uni
 que through powerful\, driving rhythms in the filthy spirit of crust punk 
 combined with snaking riffs of moody\, progressive melodies and tinged wit
 h occult psychedelia. With a sound and vision capturing the spirit and ess
 ence of the classics while forging something strange and new\, Nixil weave
 s and wanders their tortuous path in the form of surrealist black metal.\n
 \nHaving made their presence known with their 2021 independent debut\, All
  Knots Untied\, Nixil has steadily garnered a loyal following through exte
 nsive live appearances across the span of the US. Their 2023 Prosthetic Re
 cords release\, From the Wound Spilled Forth Fire\, saw them further hone 
 their craft through aural and visual presentation both on stage and record
 ing\, making the promise of their third upcoming \\(as yet untitled\\) rel
 ease a thrilling mystery. Their upcoming late spring 2025 tour marks their
  first foray out of the country\, with much more to come...
LOCATION:Arlene Francis Center for Spirit\, Art\, and Politics
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/107854018?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
