BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sourdough from Scratch with Monica Flaherty at Gold Ridge Organic 
 Farms
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T130000
UID:260505ThnSqPamjEaOL8V0a3ALWw
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a 3-hour hands-on sourdough making class at Gold R
 idge Organic Farms\, led by Monica Flaherty of the Sebastopol Sourdough Co
 mpany. Spend three immersive hours in our charming Apple Cottage learning 
 the art and science of sourdough bread making.\n\nMonica will walk you thr
 ough everything you need to know — how wild yeast and fermentation work\
 , why sourdough differs from commercial yeast bread\, and how to read your
  dough. You'll also cover starter care and feeding\, mixing and hydration 
 ratios\, shaping and scoring techniques\, and the secrets to achieving tha
 t perfect crust and open crumb.\n\nEvery guest will leave with an active s
 tarter\, a feeding schedule and care guide\, a shaped dough in a banneton 
 ready to bake at home\, and their very own apron to take home as a keepsak
 e. The experience also includes a ride across the farm on our beloved appl
 e-themed trolley to the Apple Cottage.
LOCATION:Gold Ridge Organic Farms
URL:https://www.exploretock.com/gold-ridge-organic-farms/event/606241/sour
 dough-from-scratch-with-monica-flaherty
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Spring Wine Trail
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T170000
UID:260505QmxWH6vP30ejhHzK2wyyaA
DESCRIPTION:Get ready to welcome warmer days with our Spring Wine Trail! J
 oin us for a relaxed day of wine tasting\, featuring a curated selection o
 f Whites\, Rosés\, and Sparkling wines. Perfectly paired for patio partie
 s\, beach outings\, and fun-filled moments with friends\, these wines are 
 sure to set the tone for a vibrant spring season. Warmer days call for som
 e crisp whites\, and we know you love to rosé all day—and yes\, sparkli
 ng truly does go with everything! These wineries have just the ticket to h
 elp you stock up on the perfect wines for the days ahead. For just $50\, e
 njoy a day of exploring 20 incredible wineries\, discovering hidden gems\,
  and savoring delightful wines—all without the hassle of extra fees or r
 eservations. Simply purchase your tickets online\, show them on your phone
  at each winery\, and let the adventure begin! Be sure to read through the
  program to see just what each winery will be offering for the day.
LOCATION:SCERA
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1405321074477400/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Windsor Half Marathon\, 10K\, & 5K
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T073000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T150000
UID:2605055tTGvVmA3U2GiFpSAuix8g
DESCRIPTION:With timeless qualities and a touch of small-town charm\, Wind
 sor captures the imagination of those seeking a community known for its fa
 mily-friendly environment\, wine-making heritage\, culinary delights\, and
  breathtaking vistas.\n\nThe **Half Marathon course** starts and finishes 
 on the Windsor Town Green\, winding through stunning vineyards dressed in 
 fall colors. The **10K and 5K courses** are flat\, fast\, and perfect for 
 chasing a personal record—or simply enjoying a shorter run or walk.\n\nN
 estled in the heart of the Russian River Valley\, Windsor is surrounded by
  wineries and tasting rooms where you can pair local vintages with artisan
  cheeses\, fresh-baked breads\, farm-grown produce\, and other regional de
 licacies. The town also offers a variety of welcoming restaurants\, making
  it the perfect place to savor a post-race meal.\n\nWindsor also boasts a 
 thriving craft beer scene. Home to the world-famous **Russian River Brewin
 g Company** and surrounded by Sonoma County’s bustling taprooms\, there
 ’s no shortage of opportunities to celebrate after the race.
LOCATION:Windsor Town Green 
URL:https://www.runwinecountry.com/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:36th Annual Spring Art Show
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T180000
UID:260504ha84vYFTYUWu-FeLtRZYTw
DESCRIPTION:The San Geronimo Valley Community Center presents the 36th Ann
 ual Spring Art Show from May 2–17\, 2026 in the Maurice Del Mue Gallerie
 s\,continuing a long-standing West Marin tradition that brings together ov
 er 100 local San Geronimo and Nicasio valley artists across painting\, pho
 tography\, sculpture\, printmaking\, textiles\, ceramics\, and mixed media
 .\n\n The exhibition opens with a public reception on Friday\, May 1st fr
 om 6:30–9pm featuring live music by the Old Time Music Makers. The show
  highlights the creative spirit of West Marin and the important role commu
 nity arts spaces continue to play in connecting people across generations.
 \n\n This year’s exhibition includes work by both emerging and establis
 hed artists and reflects themes of landscape\, ecology\, community\, and c
 onnection to place. The galleries will be open weekdays from 12 - 5:00pm \
 \(please call 415-488-8888 for best viewing times\\) and weekends from 12 
 -6pm. Thank you to Riley Street Art Supplies for their support and to Donn
  DeAngelo for taking the group photo and creating the poster.
LOCATION:San Geronimo Valley Community Center
URL:https://sangeronimovalleycommunitycenter.eventcalendarapp.com/36th-ann
 ual-spring-art-show
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
