BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:19 Voices in Solidarity at The Lost Church
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T190000
UID:2605029A1YAnez7UiUJfDI1yOAmA
DESCRIPTION:Bay Area musicians/songwriters are once again meeting the mome
 nt with their voices to help raise funds for peace and justice. In light o
 f the recent challenges to democracy as we know it\, Bay Area songwriter D
 eborah Crooks has organized another fundraiser featuring  women-lend musi
 cal acts to take place at The Lost Church-Santa Rosa on Saturday\, May 16\
 , 2026\, 4-7pm. This will be the fifth 19 Voices in Solidarity event\, the
  number 19 referencing the 19th Amendment which famously gave women the ri
 ght to vote in 1920. All proceeds from the show will go to the American Ci
 vil Liberties Union and the Peace and Justice Center of Sonoma County\, or
 ganizations dedicated to defending and protecting our fundamental freedoms
 .\n\nThe show will feature performances by Sonoma County and Greater Bay A
 rea-based artists including Audio Angel\, Brightdarkdawn\, Deborah Crooks\
 , Marina Crouse\, Roberta Donnay\, Aireene Espiritu\, Shockheaded Ellen\, 
 Maggie Forti\, Anna Jae\, Ellie James\, Cecilia Long\, Lindsey McFarland\,
  Megan McLaughlin\, Amy Obenski\, Sara Rodenburg\, Zoe Sameth\, Stephanie 
 Siehr\, Callie Watts  Mindi Levine\, aka ‘Mindi in the Morning\,’ fro
 m The KRUSH FM\, will serve as emcee.
LOCATION:The Lost Church
URL:https://tinyurl.com/19VoicesinSolidaritySR 
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Spring Fling at Queens Lane Sanctuary
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T160000
UID:260501xi9RPO83mES4ExbM4J3oUA
DESCRIPTION:Attention all Animal Lovers - especially Horse Lovers!\n\nQuee
 ns Lane Sanctuary in Petaluma is having their annual Spring Fling with the
  Horses. Saturday\, May 16 12 - 4 pm. Our musical talent Karen Soo Hoo wil
 l be jamming to her awesome music on guitar and you'll meet the happy hors
 es who were saved from horrific situations and who have found their foreve
 r home. Horse tours & visits\, food\, drinks\, art\, and fun area for the 
 kiddos. Silent auction and raffle. Bring your friends! Purchase tickets so
 on at www.queenslanesanctuary.org.\n\nWhether you can make it or not\, all
  donations are welcome. All proceeds go toward horses. 200 Queens Lane\, P
 etaluma\, CA\n\nFor more information\, contact Diana Avalos@QueensLaneSanc
 tuary.org
LOCATION:Queens Lane Sanctuary
URL:http://www.queenslanesanctuary.org
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:INTO THE LIGHT: Light-filled aintings by Katy Boggs
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T170000
UID:2605017MW1ClXRzUWPDwJHFcKW_A
DESCRIPTION:Katy's paintings are an exploration of light—how it shapes f
 orm\, reveals color\, and defines what we see.\n\n"I am drawn to moments w
 here light is felt as much as seen: filtering through dense leaves\, tower
 ing in the crowns of trees\, glinting off cresting waves\, or softening in
 to the quiet glow of a sunset. Light is everywhere\; without it\, there is
  no seeing. Beyond its physical presence\, it also carries a deeper resona
 nce as a symbol of hope. In a time of uncertainty\, this work seeks to bri
 ng light into the image\, both visually and metaphorically."\n\nReception:
  April 25\, 4 to 6 pm.
LOCATION:Sebastopol Gallery
URL:http://sebastopolgallery.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Our Bright Future: Clean Energy Expo
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T130000
UID:260430eljsuHLxU0WoY5_-WaeMeA
DESCRIPTION:Discover simple\, effective ways to reduce energy costs and li
 ve more sustainably at Our Bright Future: Clean Energy Expo.\n\nWhether y
 ou're interested checking out an electric vehicle or e-bike\, installing s
 olar or battery storage\, or replacing gas appliances with cleaner\, more 
 efficient electric models\, this event has you covered! Connect with exper
 ts\, explore available rebates and incentives\, and learn how to make your
  home and transportation cleaner and greener.\n\nAt the Expo\, you can:\n\
 n- Get free advice from energy efficiency and electrification experts\n\n-
  Learn about rebates and incentives for energy efficiency and electrificat
 ion projects\n\n- Watch live product demonstrations\n\n- Ask local contrac
 tors about options for solar\, battery storage\, water heaters\, HVAC\, an
 d kitchen appliances\n\n- Explore electric vehicles and e-bikes\n\n- Inves
 tigate sustainable transportation opportunities and incentives
LOCATION:Sherman Avenue
URL:https://www.novato.gov/government/sustainability/clean-energy-expo
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
