BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:You Should Be Dancing - A Tribute to the Bee Gees
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T200000
UID:2604294X4EOs5JxEa0mbKUM3B34w
DESCRIPTION:Our tribute pays homage to the Bee Gees at the peak of their f
 ame\, showcasing the energy\, creativity\, and appeal that took the world 
 by storm. You'll be treated to a night of dancing\, soaring falsettos\, an
 d some of the most beautiful ballads ever written. \n\nWhat are you waiti
 ng for? YOU should be dancing!\n\nhttps://www.bayareabeegees.com/\n\n$35.
 00 Advance & $45.00 Day of Show\n\nDoors 7pm / Show 8pm\n\nThere's somethi
 ng timeless and universally captivating about the music of the Bee Gees th
 at transcends generations. Their harmonious melodies and disco-infused cla
 ssics have made them one of the most beloved and enduring acts in music hi
 story. Now\, imagine bringing the magic of the Bee Gees to your venue\, de
 lighting your patrons with an unforgettable night of music\, dance\, and n
 ostalgia. \n\nYou Should Be Dancing is comprised of exceptionally talent
 ed musicians dedicated to faithfully recreating the Bee Gees' iconic sound
 \, while elevating the onstage visual experience. With meticulous attentio
 n to detail\, they capture the essence of the brothers Gibb\, delivering a
 n unbelievable experience that transports audiences back to the golden era
  of disco and beyond
LOCATION:Mystic Theatre & Music Hall
URL:https://wl.eventim.us/event/you-should-be-dancing-a-tribute-to-the-bee
 -gees/684648?afflky=MysticTheatre
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Redwood Writers Meeting Small But Mighty: Crafting a Winning Eleva
 tor Pitch
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T133000
UID:260428w-Q9f4PfHkuCV9TYwrdcMA
DESCRIPTION:Redwood Writers General Meeting - Lisa Manterfield: Small But 
 Mighty: Crafting a Winning Elevator Pitch\n\n**When and Where:**\n\n**May 
 16\, 2026\, 11 a.m. Finley Center in Santa Rosa**\n\nPlease bring somethin
 g savory or sweet to share in our potluck!\n\n“So\, what’s your book a
 bout?” It’s a simple question that strikes terror in many writers. How
  do you condense your 300-page masterpiece into a few sentences without ma
 king your audience’s eyes glaze over? In this class\, you’ll learn the
  key elements that will draw the reader in and make your story feel both u
 nique and universal. Plus\, you’ll see how this short piece of sales cop
 y forms the foundation of your query letter\, book jacket copy\, and more.
  Come with your latest book premise and leave with a winning pitch.\n\n**A
 bout the Presenter:** Lisa Manterfield is the award-winning author of five
  novels and two works of non-fiction\, including *All Our Lies Are True*\
 , a psychological suspense that Publishers Weekly calls “gut-wrenching
 …and legitimately gripping.” As a book coach and editor\, she loves to
  help writers take their work to the next level and is a regular instructo
 r for Stanford Continuing Studies Creative Writing program. Originally fro
 m northern England\, she now lives in Northern California with her husband
  and cat. When not writing\, she can be found hiking in the redwoods and d
 igging in her vegetable garden. Her new mystery novel\, *Invisible Ink*\,
  will be published by Thomas & Mercer in 2027.\n\nLearn more at LisaMante
 rfield.com\, or say hello on Instagram or Facebook
LOCATION:Finley Center
URL:https://redwoodwriters.org/may-2026-lisa-manterfield/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
