BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Finding Lucinda Film Screening and Songwriter Round
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T000000
UID:260315luo8gBLM7kuaG9t_q7C9nQ
DESCRIPTION:A documentary screening and live performance of Lucinda Willia
 ms music.\n\nSaturday\, May 16\n\nDoors: 7:30pm\n\nDance Palace Church Spa
 ce\n\nWine\, Beer\, and Refreshments available for purchase\n\nAll Sales F
 inal\n\nMusic lovers and Lucinda Williams fans are invited to an inspiring
  event that blends live performance\, documentary screening\, and conversa
 tion as Finding Lucinda comes to The Dance Palace. This show celebrates th
 e early life\, creative spark\, and lasting influence of the legendary sin
 ger-songwriter Lucinda Williams. To start the event\, ISMAY and Kelly McFa
 rling will be performing Lucinda Williams songs.\n\nFinding Lucinda \\(fil
 m\\) follows singer-songwriter ISMAY \\(Avery Hellman\\) on a transformati
 ve road trip through the American South\, exploring the early life and end
 uring legacy of three-time GRAMMY-winning artist Lucinda Williams. Along t
 he way\, the film features never-before-seen footage\, rare recordings\, a
 nd interviews with Charlie Sexton\, Buddy Miller\, Mary Gauthier\, and Luc
 inda herself.\n\nwww.findinglucinda.com
LOCATION:Dance Palace
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/107983439?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:GUIDE DOGS FOR THE BLIND'S GRADUATION CEREMONIES MELT HEARTS
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T143000
UID:260314gObdgUT1R0SM06MvnBF22Q
DESCRIPTION:Guide Dogs for the Blind \\(GDB\\) will celebrate its guide d
 og team graduates every other Saturday with public graduation ceremonies a
 t the organization’s campus in San Rafael. These touching public events 
 have inspired tears in even the most stoic audience members\, as graduatin
 g guide dog teams proudly take the stage. Families are welcome at the cere
 monies\, which honor the independence and companionship that GDB’s gui
 de dogs provide for GDB’s clients who are blind or visually impaired. T
 he events also allow GDB’s clients to meet the puppy raisers who cared 
 for their canine heroes prior to beginning formal training at GDB’s cam
 pus. Ceremonies also recognize recent graduates of GDB’s Orientation an
 d Mobility \\(O&M\\) Program\, K9 Buddy Program\, and Breeder Dog Program
 .\n\nAdmission is free\, and Kleenex will be provided. Pre-registered bus 
 groups are welcome. Public tours of the campus are offered on the days of 
 the ceremonies. Visit www.guidedogs.com for more information. Graduat
 ion events are also livestreamed at https://www.youtube.com/@gdb\\_offici
 al/streams.
LOCATION:Guide Dogs for the Blind
URL:https://www.guidedogs.com/about-guide-dogs-for-the-blind/graduations
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Neighborhood Table 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T210000
UID:260310tdA9c646GkebiGH-m9yFdw
DESCRIPTION:The Neighborhood Table is proud to support the St. Helena Hosp
 ital Foundation’s Mobile Health team\, a pioneering initiative in Napa C
 ounty. This innovative program delivers essential healthcare services dire
 ctly to the most vulnerable populations in Napa Valley\, including farmwor
 kers\, homebound residents\, and others facing barriers such as cost\, tra
 nsportation\, language\, and technology.\n\nIn 2025\, the Mobile Health te
 am continued to make a powerful impact\, distributing over 62\,123 pounds 
 of fresh produce to families in need. They served more than 500 individual
 s monthly at key locations in Calistoga\, St. Helena\, and Napa\, and host
 ed 35 community events that reached over 18\,446 people\, including 853 se
 niors. By partnering with trusted local organizations such as Up Valley Fa
 mily Center and Puertas Abiertas\, they ensured care and resources reached
  those who needed it most.\n\nThanks to your support\, the team also condu
 cted 1\,049 health assessments —measuring vital indicators such as blood
  pressure\, A1c\, and cholesterol—and provided more than 100 sports phys
 icals for local high school students. They administered nearly 2\,000 vacc
 ines\, including 1\,175 COVID-19 doses\, 700 flu shots\, and 77 RSV vaccin
 es\, helping safeguard public health across the county.\n\nWith your conti
 nued support\, we look forward to expanding these efforts even further in 
 2026—bringing critical healthcare and food resources to underserved comm
 unities throughout Napa County.\n\nPlease join us at Neighborhood Table 20
 26 as we come together to build a healthier\, more supportive community fo
 r seniors\, families\, and neighbors in need across the Napa Valley.
LOCATION:Adams St. at Library Lane
URL:https://shhfoundation.org/special-events/neighborhood-table/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
