BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:What We Inherit\, What We Create: Collage as Reflection
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T160000
UID:2605139i4kyJ9_XUShV4BNijm8uA
DESCRIPTION:In dialogue with our upcoming Origin Stories exhibition\, this
  workshop uses found imagery\, vintage ephemera\, and contemporary materia
 ls to reflect on memory\, place\, and the textures of everyday life. Parti
 cipants will create layered works that balance personal narrative with bro
 ader cultural reference. Emphasis will be placed on editing\, composition\
 , and allowing materials to suggest meaning rather than working toward a f
 ixed outcome. All experience levels are welcome. \n\nInstructors: Robin Bo
 relli\, Laura Engdahl\, and Jen Siddens \n\nMaterials: Two 12&rdquo\; x 12
 &rdquo\; wood panels and heavy art paper are provided and included in the 
 price.  A supply list of other art supplies for participants to bring will
  be provided upon registration. Participants are also encouraged to bring 
 copies of personal photographs\, letters\, maps\, or printed matter that f
 eel connected to their own sense of personal history\, though some shared 
 collage materials will also be provided.\n\nCost: $150 Members\, $170 Non-
 members  
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/what-we-inherit-what-we-cr
 eate-collage-as-reflecti?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
