BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Donovan Plant
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T000000
UID:260327FU-oOyugsEGrEr_vIUC9VQ
DESCRIPTION:Former San Francisco private detective Donovan Plant spent nea
 rly two decades chasing leads and tailing cheaters before returning to his
  musical roots.  Donovan Plant blends rock\, country and pop with lyrics i
 nspired by the city.\n\nCiting influences such as David Bowie\, The Cars\,
  and Jackson Brown\, Donovan’s keen ear for hooks and melody is on full 
 display with NIGHT FEEL GOOD\, recorded inside the world-famous Hyde Stree
 t Studios at Dreamrack Studios by producer and engineer Trent Berry. \n\nD
 onovan formed DONOVAN PLANT & THE LEAFS in 2018\, a group that includes dr
 ummer Lliam Hart \\(Information Society/Wire Train\\)\, bassist Mike Henry
  \\(Minus One\\) and lead guitarist Jason Rojek \\(Sugar Crash\\). Lliam\,
  Mike\, and Jason have been playing live and recording together for years.
  When Lliam joined with Donovan for some live shows about ten years ago\, 
 he quickly recognized Donovan’s talent for song writing and quietly set 
 about a plan to incorporate his friend Mike into the band\, a plan which w
 orked brilliantly. In a stroke of mis-spelling genius they then named this
  creation THE LEAFS. \n\n Donovan has released three solo EP’s\, Be With
  You \\(Niteflite Music - Germany\\) with producer Fabian Gorg in 2011\, w
 hich included a video produced by Ricky Kelley\, City Lights \\(Angel Blos
 som Records\\) with producer Scott Mickelson in 2018 and Night Feel Good \
 \(Angel Blossom Records\\) with producer Trent Berry at the historic Hyde 
 Street Studios \\(Dreamrack Studios\\).  He also had the honor of playing 
 inside San Quentin State Prison as part of its annual Day of Peacecelebrat
 ions with the non-profit organization Bread & Roses Presents for two conse
 cutive years in 2016 and 2017.
LOCATION:Head West at the Barlow
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108081487?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
