SUMMARY:Flora & Fauna - 6
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T160000
UID:260225VhwJvQrIp0Cc_Dy_CBJ7Tw
DESCRIPTION:In this 6 week course\, participants will learn a unique appro
 ach to watercolor\, intended to alleviate the frustration that many experi
 ence when learning this beautiful yet challenging medium. The class will f
 ocus on strengthening one’s observational skills\, giving the artist a f
 oundation off of which to build their paintings in a step by step layering
  process\, that trains the artist to see value and color\n\nOur subjects w
 ill be flora and fauna - a sampling of plants and animals - fruits\, flora
 ls\, foliage\, and four legged friends. These subjects are great for begin
 ners and experienced watercolor painters alike\; their organic shapes make
  them forgiving drawing subjects\, but their beauty can be a muse for life
 . \n\nThis class will work from life and from photos\, practicing basic d
 rawing skills in addition to watercolor technique. With six class sessions
 \, participants will have the opportunity to develop their skills and buil
 d muscle memory with a medium that often feels like it has a mind of its o
 wn.\n\nAll materials provided.\n\nLocation: 755 Petaluma Ave\, Sebastopol\
 , CA\n\nDates: 6 Sundays - May 17\, 24\, 31\, June 7\, 14\, 21\n\nTime: 1 
 - 4 pm\n\nRegistration Fee: $300\n\nAges: Adults\n\nSkill Level: All Level
 s
LOCATION:Art & Soul Sebastopol
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/flora-fauna-6/18187343/
 2026-05-17T13
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Off-Grid Printing Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T130000
UID:260216GCsW3tXG5UezhXT33YLtbw
DESCRIPTION:In this two session workshop\, students will work hands-on wit
 h metal and wood type to create off-grid compositions—playing with spaci
 ng\, rotation\, fragmentation\, overlap\, and improvisation. We’ll explo
 re how imbalance\, disruption\, and intuition can shape meaning\, rhythm\,
  and visual impact in printed work.\n\nThis class emphasizes process over 
 perfection. Expect to test ideas\, make quick prints\, respond to chance\,
  and let the material qualities of type and press guide the work.\n\nSuita
 ble for curious beginners and experienced printers alike\, this workshop o
 ffers a supportive space to experiment\, loosen habits\, and discover new 
 possibilities in letterpress printing beyond the grid.\n\nAll materials pr
 ovided. No prior letterpress experience required\, though comfort with bas
 ic printing concepts is helpful.
LOCATION:North Bay Letterpress Arts
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/off-grid-printing-works
 hop/18131360/2026-05-17T10
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Comics and Visual Storytelling with Paige Braddock and Mary Shyne
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T193000
UID:260505es6LIZz120aYVMX6ml5Dgg
DESCRIPTION:Comics and Visual Storytelling Join Paige Braddock and Mary Sh
 yne as they talk about creating graphic novels for both young adults and e
 arly readers. They will be sharing excerpts from their most recent work an
 d talking about character and story development. Free event. Refreshments 
 for sale\, book sales & author signing. Audience Q&A.   Paige Braddock is 
 an award-winning creator and Creative Director Emeritus at Charles M. Schu
 lz's Studio in Santa Rosa. Her graphic novels for kids include Stinky Ceci
 l and Peanut\, Butter\, & Crackers\, which won a Beverly Cleary Children's
  Choice Award. And have been translated into multiple languages. The fifth
  book in the Peanut\, Butter\, & Crackers series\, Christmas Surprise\, wa
 s recently released by Nosy Crow in the UK and Greece. Paige's Eisner-nomi
 nated comic strip\, Jane's World\, was the first gay-themed comic work to 
 receive online distribution by a national media syndicate in the U.S. The 
 comic strip compled its 20-year run in 2018.   Mary Shyne is a Chicago-are
 a native\, who spent a decade in New York working in publishing before get
 ting her MFA at the Center for Cartoon Studies. She currently lives in the
  Bay Area where she works on all things Snoopy at Charles M Schulz's Studi
 o. Mary's debut graphic novel\, You and Me on Repeat\, was nominated for t
 he ALA's William C. Morris Award and named a Best Book of 2025 by New York
  Public Libr
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts
URL:https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/comics-and-
 visual-storytelling-with-paige-braddock-and-mary-shyne
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
