BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:INTO THE LIGHT: Light-filled aintings by Katy Boggs
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260519T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260519T170000
UID:260501h86lWT3KUUu-j41deXV7XA
DESCRIPTION:Katy's paintings are an exploration of light—how it shapes f
 orm\, reveals color\, and defines what we see.\n\n"I am drawn to moments w
 here light is felt as much as seen: filtering through dense leaves\, tower
 ing in the crowns of trees\, glinting off cresting waves\, or softening in
 to the quiet glow of a sunset. Light is everywhere\; without it\, there is
  no seeing. Beyond its physical presence\, it also carries a deeper resona
 nce as a symbol of hope. In a time of uncertainty\, this work seeks to bri
 ng light into the image\, both visually and metaphorically."\n\nReception:
  April 25\, 4 to 6 pm.
LOCATION:Sebastopol Gallery
URL:http://sebastopolgallery.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Modern Monks\, Timeless Wisdom
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260519T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260519T203000
UID:260430f3eolJQj80mnPctv0Oscaw
DESCRIPTION:with Kovilo Bhikkhu and Ajahn Nisabho\n\nJoin us for this even
 ing of meditation\, talk\, and discussion with two engaging young monks fr
 om Seattle\, Ajahn Kovilo and Ajahn Nisabho. Both have been ordained for m
 any years in the Thai Forest lineage of Ajahn Chah and have trained in mon
 asteries in Thailand and the US. They are unique as monks in hosting a wee
 kly podcast on their YouTube channel \\(https://www.youtube.com/@ClearMoun
 tainMonastery/podcasts\\) with noted Buddhist teachers\, including Jack Ko
 rnfield and Joseph Goldstein. They have a large lay community in Seattle s
 upporting their plans for a new forest monastery within driving distance o
 f the city.\n\nIn this evening program you will hear more about these monk
 s’ backgrounds and receive fresh teachings in the classical style of Aja
 hn Chah. While the monks are well known to Insight practitioners in the Se
 attle area\, this will be their first visit to Spirit Rock—but not their
  last.
LOCATION:Spirit Rock Meditation Center
URL:https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/modern-monks-timeless-
 wisdom-aa1g26/?lang=en
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Marcus Rezak
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260519T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260519T000000
UID:260429aZOj7LOSxECSNNweUyCGhw
DESCRIPTION:Marcus Rezak is a dynamic guitarist and vocalist known for fus
 ing blues roots with jam-driven improvisation and songwriting. His latest 
 album Guitar Head\, produced by GRAMMY-winner Paul Nelson and released via
  Deko Entertainment/ADA-Warner\, showcases a bold new direction—melding 
 Chicago blues with modern psychedelia and funk. The record features top-ti
 er players including Ray Paczkowski \\(TAB\\)\, Adrian Tramontano \\(Twidd
 le\\)\, Chris DeAngelis \\(Kung Fu\\)\, and Erik Lawrence \\(Little Feat\\
 ).\n\nRezak’s recent highlights include performances with Blues Traveler
 \, LP Giobbi\, DJ Logic\, G. Love\, and a high-energy set at Brooklyn Bowl
  supporting Dumpstaphunk. His live shows\, musical vision\, and collaborat
 ive spirit continue to make him a standout force on stage and in the studi
 o.\n\n“Marcus is a force to be reckoned with… this album showcases his
  diversity and amazing talent.”\n\n— Paul Nelson \\(GRAMMY-winning pro
 ducer/guitarist\\)\n\nAs a guitar instructor\, he built his own freelance 
 clientele\, teaching primarily Jazz students\, but also having no limitati
 ons to this as well. Marcus Rezak has a B.M. from Berklee College of Music
  in Boston\, and a M.M. degree in Jazz Composition from DePaul University 
 in Chicago\, IL.\n\n"The story of Marcus Rezak is not one for those who do
 n’t believe in fated occurrences or natural affinity. It is not for thos
 e who don’t believe that passion should forcefully direct the flow of on
 e’s life. It is\, however\, a tale for seekers ready to leave misgivings
  at the door and allow music’s sway to settle in their minds like a rich
  fog. In music\, we find truth. Within music’s truth\, we find the sound
 s of Marcus Rezak."
LOCATION:Golden gate bistro
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108252237?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Private Screening of American Graffiti with 60’s Diner Dinner at
  Costeaux
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260519T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260519T210000
UID:260422atFx89vmPEa6GqCar-jETg
DESCRIPTION:Come dressed in your best greaser style and step back in time 
 for this throwback evening. Enjoy a 1960s‑inspired dinner at Costeaux 
 French Bakery—which has served as Healdsburg's Bakery for over 100 years
 . The dinner will take place from 5:30-6:45pm\, and will include classic b
 urgers and fries\, root beer floats\, and wine and beer. There will also b
 e vintage cars on display outside\, so you can truly travel back in time.
  \n\nAfter dinner\, head to Healdsburg's film hub\, True West Film Center
 \, for a private 7:15pm screening of George Lucas and Francis Ford Coppola
 's coming-of-age classic\, American Graffiti. Filmed in Petaluma\, this 19
 73 film perfectly encapsulates the sights\, sounds\, and spirit of 1960s A
 merica. Concessions will also be available for all attendees. \n\n**Our s
 incere gratitude to True West Film Center for making this experience possi
 ble.** \n\n100% of proceeds from this event go to Boys & Girls Clubs of So
 noma-Marin. These funds support us in providing after-school programs\, su
 mmer camps\, and essential resources for 11\,000 local youth—at Clubs fr
 om Geyserville to Petaluma. \n\n**Ticket sales for this event are live an
 d close on Sunday\, April 26th at 6pm.**
LOCATION:Costeaux French Bakery
URL:https://hbginbloom2026.ggo.bid/n/package/15104468
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
