BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:IN A LANDSCAPE: Classical Music in the Wild™
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260522T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260522T183000
UID:260314YBuO3o33IUeKUCJiBsM1iw
DESCRIPTION:For the fifth year\, classical pianist and naturalist Hunter N
 oack will bring IN A LANDSCAPE: Classical Music in the Wild™ to Jack Lon
 don State Historic Park. \n\nOn May 22 and 23\, the groundbreaking concer
 t series will transform how audiences experience classical music by removi
 ng it from the confines of traditional concert halls and placing it in the
  great outdoors.\n\nVineyards\, redwood forests\, and sunny meadows will r
 eplace the traditional concert hall as audiences listen through state-of-t
 he-art wireless headphones\, wandering freely with the music as a soundtra
 ck to their experience.\n\nThe concerts at Jack London State Historic Park
  will be performed at 5-6:30 p.m. in the winery ruins. Attendees are encou
 raged to arrive early to enjoy the park\, bring a picnic and favorite beve
 rages\, plus lawn chairs or blankets to sit on (seating is not provided).
   \n\nDuring the concert\, the headsets will carry the music throughout 
 the meadow\, the historic winery ruins and around the Londons’ cottage a
 nd barns.\n\nFor more information about IN A LANDSCAPE visit www.inalandsc
 ape.org.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/in-a-landscape-classical-music-in-th
 e-wild-2026-night1/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Callie Watts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260522T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260522T000000
UID:260227idx4Y7qIvEyOQctqUMZqpg
DESCRIPTION:Callie Watts is a singer/songwriter from Northern California w
 ho was raised on classical music\, The Beatles and The Beach Boys before d
 iscovering Joni Mitchell\, Elton John\, Stevie Wonder\, Paul Simon\, Billy
  Joel\, Carole King\, and all the great writers of the ’60s and 70’s w
 ho have influenced her sound and writing style. After graduating high scho
 ol\, Callie began playing and performing solo\, as well as in local and ba
 y area bands of different genres. She’s played blues with Eric Lindell a
 nd the Reds\, funky soul with Phatty\, and jazz/swing with Savoy Swingers 
 along with many other various projects. Callie has taken turns throughout 
 her career as a keyboardist\, guitarist\, writer\, and lead/backing vocali
 st\, and she’s currently a member of the dynamic Sonoma County funk rock
  band Burrows and Dilbeck\, having joined in 2010 as part of the former ba
 nd Frobeck. Over time\, she’s had the honor of opening for acts such as 
 Bootsy Collins\, Elvin Bishop\, Huey Lewis and The News\, War\, Ozomatli\,
  Bill Champlin\, Booker T\, and the B52s. Callie continues to perform freq
 uently as an acoustic solo artist\, focusing on developing a core audience
