BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Drawing Trees in Mixed Media: A Day at Jack London Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T150000
UID:260405umkWUKfJhUielFVdu9o4RA
DESCRIPTION:Spend a day immersed in the art of drawing trees\, set against
  the inspiring landscape of Jack London State Historic Park. Presented in 
 partnership with the Sonoma Community Center\, This plein air workshop ble
 nds skill-building with outdoor observation\, helping you deepen both your
  technique and your connection to the natural world.\n\nIn the morning\, f
 ocus on foundational drawing principles—learning how to capture accurate
  proportions\, simplify complex forms\, and develop a strong sense of valu
 e.\n\nIn the afternoon\, attention shifts to the expressive qualities of t
 rees\, exploring texture\, color\, and light as observed directly from the
  landscape. Enhance your drawings with watercolor washes\, adding depth\, 
 atmosphere\, and color to bring trees to life. Step-by-step guidance ensur
 es that finished piece reflects both structure and character.\n\nBring a p
 icnic lunch for a mid-day break\, and a lightweight folding chair if you h
 ave one (seating is also available at picnic tables\, benches\, or on the 
 ground). All materials are provided.  Artists of all experience levels ar
 e welcome!
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/plein-air-trees-may-2026/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
