BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:IN A LANDSCAPE: Classical Music in the Wild™
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T050000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T183000
UID:2603156eBrgnE1w0iqR2OvOsfP4w
DESCRIPTION:For the fifth year\, classical pianist and naturalist Hunter N
 oack will bring IN A LANDSCAPE: Classical Music in the Wild™ to Jack Lon
 don State Historic Park. \n\nOn May 22 and 23\, the groundbreaking concer
 t series will transform how audiences experience classical music by removi
 ng it from the confines of traditional concert halls and placing it in the
  great outdoors.\n\nVineyards\, redwood forests\, and sunny meadows will r
 eplace the traditional concert hall as audiences listen through state-of-t
 he-art wireless headphones\, wandering freely with the music as a soundtra
 ck to their experience.\n\nThe concerts at Jack London State Historic Park
  will be performed at 5-6:30 p.m. in the winery ruins. Attendees are encou
 raged to arrive early to enjoy the park\, bring a picnic and favorite beve
 rages\, plus lawn chairs or blankets to sit on (seating is not provided).
   \n\nDuring the concert\, the headsets will carry the music throughout 
 the meadow\, the historic winery ruins and around the Londons’ cottage a
 nd barns.\n\nFor more information about IN A LANDSCAPE visit www.inalandsc
 ape.org.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/in-a-landscape-classical-music-in-th
 e-wild-2026-night2/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
