BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Slow Birding Journey
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260524T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260524T160000
UID:260425yUc5SD5TLkuYskzYS7Wtxg
DESCRIPTION:Do you enjoy a slow walk in a valley\, breezes\, wil
 dflowers\, the sounds of songbirds\, the taste of a Douglas Fir
  needle or a California Bay leaf\, the aroma of Tarweed\, or w
 atching wild turkeys and California Quail hunt for seeds and ins
 ects in the grass  Each month \\(weather permitting\\) we will e
 xplore one or two of our three accessible trails-- the Creekside
  Trail\, the Nature Trail\, and the Meadow trail. Suitable for 
 all levels and a range of mobility\, these Sunday afternoon adve
 ntures will accommodate people using walkers or wheelchairs\, youn
 g children\, parents with babies in strollers\, as well as those
  who just enjoy slow walks in nature that stimulate the five s
 enses. \n\nOur May outing will focus on the birds of Sugarloaf.
  Tickets are $5 for adults and free for children under 18 year
 s of age. All minors must be accompanied by parent or legal gu
 ardian. Tickets day-of\, on site will be $10 and might not be 
 available. Meet at the White Barn parking lot. \n\nThere will be
  frequent stops and opportunities for conversation\, photography\,
  nature journaling\, wildlife viewing\, resting\, etc.\, so bring
  your nature journal\, camera\, or binoculars if you have them.
  Wear comfortable shoes\, a hat\, sun protection\, bring water a
 nd if desired\, a snack. Parking fees apply
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/2026-mayjourn
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:In a Landscape - Classical Music in the Wild
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260524T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260524T170000
UID:2604255IeKE6AqVEqr5Q8-4T3dZA
DESCRIPTION:For the 11th season\, IN A LANDSCAPE: Classical Music in the W
 ild tours the American West. Mountain tops\, old-growth forests\, and sunn
 y meadows replace the traditional concert hall in the series featuring pia
 nist Hunter Noack on a 9-foot Steinway concert grand piano. Listen through
  wireless headphones and wander afield with the music as a soundtrack to y
 our experience in the wild.\n\nAbout this Landscape\n\nSet along a gentle 
 creek in the tiny hamlet of Hopland\, Campovida is a family-owned farm and
  winery. Lavender gardens guide guests to the concert site\, a meadow fram
 ed by a pair of oak trees. Organic and biodynamic farming practices connec
 t the 150 acres of orchards and gardens to the rich agricultural legacy of
  the Pomo people in the ancestral Sanel Valley of southeastern Mendocino C
 ounty.\n\nTurn your concert into a wine-country weekend with a stay at Tha
 tcher Hotel or Stock Farm Hotel\, both located just one mile from Campovid
 a in Hopland. Explore nearby wineries\, restaurants\, and small-town shops
  with guidance from Visit Ukiah as you plan your visit.\n\nWith thanks to 
 Thatcher Hotel\, Stock Farm Hotel\, and Visit Ukiah for their support of t
 his concert.\n\nConcert FAQs:\n\nAccessibilityThe pathway to the concert s
 ite\, will be approximately a 15 minute walk from a paved parking lot\, to
  a dirt path\, through an organic garden and field with some uneven terrai
 n.\n\nSeatingBring your own chairs or blankets.No seating provided.\n\nFoo
 d & BeveragesDrinks and light snacks will be available for purchase. Outsi
 de food and drink are not permitted.\n\nDogsNot allowed at Campovida Winer
 y.\n\nSmokingProhibited at all IN A LANDSCAPE concert sites.\n\nRefunds & 
 CancellationsAll ticket purchases are final. There are no refunds unless I
 N A LANDSCAPE cancels the performance. The show goes on regardless of weat
 her.
LOCATION:Campovida
URL:https://visitukiah.com/events/in-a-landscape-classical-music-in-the-wi
 ld/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
