BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Charley Crockett - Age of the Ram Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260524T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260524T193000
UID:2604127oIjzqMA-EqadYXkE-9WQQ
DESCRIPTION:Back to All Shows\n\nCharley Crockett – Age of the Ram Tour 
 with Special Guest Alicia Blue\n\nSunday\, May 24\, 2026\n\n7:30 pm\n\nBUY
  TICKETS \n\n🔑 Featuring a pre‑show Club for membership levels $500\\
 +. Click here for info. \n\nCharley Crockett has carved out a singular pla
 ce in modern country music by refusing to play by the rules. A wanderer tu
 rned street singer turned chart-climbing songwriter\, he’s built a caree
 r on instinct\, independence\, and a deep reverence for the renegade tradi
 tion of artists like Willie Nelson\, Waylon Jennings\, and Gram Parsons. F
 resh off the release of Age of the Ram\, the final chapter of his Sagebrus
 h Trilogy\, Crockett arrives with a new batch of songs that paint a vivid 
 picture of his journey from Texas dreamer\, New York street singer\, and t
 wice-convicted felon to the belly of the country music beast. \n\nThis is 
 Crockett’s vision of hard country music. Guitar and pedal steel are the 
 rule on the album\, often accompanied by piano\, harmonica\, and keys. Pro
 duced by Shooter Jennings\, the record leans into hard country textures—
 guitar\, pedal steel\, harmonica\, and the dusty atmosphere of an old west
 ern film. Crockett threads narrative tracks\, character studies\, and clas
 sic covers into a vivid frontier tale\, punctuated by moments of introspec
 tion that reveal the man behind the myth. \n\nCharley Crockett\, in partne
 rship with PLUS1\, will contribute $1.00 from every ticket sold to Last P
 risoner Project\, a 501\\(c\\)\\(3\\) organization\, to support efforts to
  free individuals incarcerated for cannabis-related offenses and repair th
 e harms of the war on cannabis. Founded in 2019\, Last Prisoner Project wo
 rks nationwide to advance cannabis justice and advocate for policies that 
 repair the harms of cannabis prohibition. Charley Crockett is proud to sup
 port this work and help raise awareness in communities across the country.
  For more information\, visit LastPrisonerProject.org. No portion of the 
 ticket purchase is tax deductible.\n\n \n\nTHIRD PARTY RESELLERS\n\nDon’
 t get taken by deceptive online resellers who use bots to buy tickets and 
 then mark up their prices. The only safe way to protect your purchase and 
 guarantee the best seats at the lowest cost is to work directly with us: t
 hrough our website\, by phone\, or at our box office in Santa Rosa. Plus\,
  we’re not bots. Our friendly team members are easily accessible by phon
 e or at the box office to provide customer support.
LOCATION:Luther Burbank Center for the Arts
URL:https://lutherburbankcenter.org/event/charley-crockett/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
