DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260530T163000
UID:260425kaWrgp9I4Uu1uujFAYvqfg
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to save a life!\n\nFocusing on recognizing and treat
 ing life-threatening situations in the critical minutes before 911 arrives
 \, we will cover how to handle adult and infant cardiac arrest\, choking\,
  heart attack\, severe bleeding and more! We'll be using modern manikins a
 nd equipment in a small-group setting\, answering questions along the way.
 \n\nYour American Red Cross certificate will be valid for 2 years. This is
  a blended course: Watch the videos and presentations online at your own c
 onvenience before joining your patient and friendly instructor to practice
  your new skills!\n\n(This community class event is held at a branch of So
 noma County Library. We thank them for their hospitality. They have reques
 ted that we mention that this program is neither sponsored by nor affiliat
 ed with the Sonoma County Library. Done!)\n\nPlease get in touch with any 
 questions!
LOCATION:Sebastopol Regional Library
URL:https://riverpreparedfirstaid.com/community-classes/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
