BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sashiko Embroidery & Visible Mending with Lena Wolff
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260607T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260607T150000
UID:260513LiUlPMrKR0yYZdwMzOjhfA
DESCRIPTION:This workshop offers an introduction to hand-sewing and Sashik
 o\, a meditative form of embroidery that encompasses a vast lexicon of lyr
 ical and geometric patterns that developed in Japan in the mid-1600's. All
  skill levels are welcome to join\, from absolute beginners to those with 
 some experience or for people who have taken a workshop with me in the pas
 t.\n\nA brief history and the basic principles of Sashiko will be introduc
 ed\, including how to read and draft patterns onto fabric by hand with eas
 e. In the intimate setting of my studio with a small class size\, particip
 ants can chose to work on a variety of possible projects\, with fabric pre
 pared to make coasters\, sachets\, or patches with visible mending.\n\nAll
  materials will be provided\, including naturally dyed Sashiko thread made
  by A Verb for Keeping Warm\, along with resources to take home to springb
 oard future projects to embellish clothing\, quilts\, or other home textil
 es.\n\n$220 includes $20 materials fee\n\nLena Wolff is a Bay Area&ndash\;
 based artist\, craftswoman\, and democracy activist whose work draws from 
 folk traditions\, geometric abstraction\, and social practice\, spanning d
 rawing\, collage\, sculpture\, and public projects. In 2017\, she founded 
 Art for Democracy\, a nationally recognized initiative promoting civic eng
 agement through art. Her work has been exhibited widely and is held in maj
 or collections including the San Francisco Museum of Modern Art and Berkel
 ey Art Museum. She lives in Berkeley with her wife\, artist Miriam Klein S
 tahl\, and their daughter.\n\nMain website: www.lenawolff.comArt for Democ
 racy website: https://www.art-for-democracy.org/Workshops: https://lenawol
 ff.com/shop
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/sashiko-embroidery-visible
 -mending-with-lena-wolff?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
